---
import { brandSettings } from '../../scripts/brandSettings.js';
---
<section id="typography">
                <h2>Typography</h2>
                

                <h3>Typeface Selection</h3>
                <p><strong>Primary Typeface:</strong> {brandSettings.typography.primaryFont}</p>
                <p><strong>Secondary Typeface:</strong> {brandSettings.typography.secondaryFont}</p>
                <p><strong>Tertiary Typeface:</strong> {brandSettings.typography.tertiaryFont}</p>
                
                <h3>Readability Standards</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Line Height:</strong> Body text must have a line height of at least {brandSettings.typography.lineHeight} to ensure readability.</li>
                    <li><strong>Paragraph Spacing:</strong> Spacing between paragraphs must be at least {brandSettings.typography.paragraphSpacing} times the font size.</li>
                    <li><strong>Alignment:</strong> Body text should be left aligned for readibility reasons. Text justification should be avoided because it typiccally creates rivers and makes the text hard to read. Right or center alignment may be okay for headings or short phrases, but overall text should be aligned to the left.</li>
                    <li><strong>Capitalization:</strong> Sans Serif headings may be put in all caps, but it's not preferable. For body text is should be avoided.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Hierarchy Preview</h3>
                <div class="type-preview">
                    <h1>Heading 1 (H1) - [30px/Regular]</h1>
                    <h2>Heading 2 (H2) - [24px/Regular]</h2>
                    <h3>Heading 3 (H3) - [20px/Regular]</h3>
                    <p>Body Paragraph - [16px/Regular]. This demonstrates how the standard reading text will look. [State your minimum body text size requirement here, and add a sample passage].</p>
                </div>
            </section>